{"id":"mahabharata-7-010","work":"mahabharata","part":7,"partName":"द्रोणपर्व","partNameEn":"Drona Parva","unit":10,"title":"दशमोऽध्यायः","titleEn":"Adhyaya 10 · The deeds of Krishna","summary":{"en":"Dhritarashtra recounts the divine deeds of Vasudeva from his childhood among the cowherds, his killing of Kamsa and Shishupala, and his boundless virtues. He concludes that Duryodhana's folly in opposing him has brought this ruin.","kn":"ಧೃತರಾಷ್ಟ್ರ ವಾಸುದೇವನ ಬಾಲ್ಯದ ಗೋಪಕುಲದ ದಿವ್ಯ ಕಾರ್ಯಗಳು, ಕಂಸ-ಶಿಶುಪಾಲರ ವಧೆ, ಅಪಾರ ಗುಣಗಳನ್ನು ಹೇಳುತ್ತಾನೆ. ಅವನನ್ನು ವಿರೋಧಿಸಿದ ದುರ್ಯೋಧನನ ಮೂರ್ಖತನವೇ ಈ ನಾಶ ತಂದಿತೆಂದು ತೀರ್ಮಾನಿಸುತ್ತಾನೆ.","hi":"धृतराष्ट्र वासुदेव के गोपकुल में बचपन के दिव्य कर्म, कंस और शिशुपाल का वध और अपार गुण सुनाते हैं। वे निष्कर्ष निकालते हैं कि उनके विरोध की दुर्योधन की मूर्खता से यह विनाश आया।","te":"ధృతరాష్ట్రుడు వాసుదేవుని గోపకులంలోని బాల్య దివ్యకార్యాలు, కంస శిశుపాల వధలు, అపార గుణాలను వివరిస్తాడు. ఆయనను వ్యతిరేకించిన దుర్యోధనుని మూర్ఖత్వమే ఈ నాశనానికి కారణమని తేలుస్తాడు.","ta":"த்ருதராஷ்டிரன் வாசுதேவனின் ஆயர்குலச் சிறு பிராயத்துத் தெய்வச் செயல்கள், கம்ச சிசுபாலர் வதம், அளவற்ற குணங்களைக் கூறுகிறான். அவரை எதிர்த்த துரியோதனனின் மடமையே இந்த அழிவைத் தந்தது என்று முடிக்கிறான்.","ml":"ഇടയന്മാർക്കിടയിൽ ബാല്യം മുതലുള്ള വാസുദേവന്റെ ദിവ്യകൃത്യങ്ങളും കംസന്റെയും ശിശുപാലന്റെയും വധവും അനന്തമായ ഗുണങ്ങളും ധൃതരാഷ്ട്രർ ഓർമിക്കുന്നു. അദ്ദേഹത്തെ എതിർത്ത ദുര്യോധനന്റെ മൂഢതയാണ് ഈ നാശത്തിന് കാരണമെന്ന് അദ്ദേഹം നിഗമനത്തിലെത്തുന്നു."},"source":"Mahabharata, Critical Edition (BORI, Pune) 7.10; e-text by M. Tokunaga and J. D. Smith, © BORI 1999, version of Tue Sep 22 2026","sections":[{"title":"द्रोणाभिषेकपर्व","titleEn":"Dronabhisheka Parva (Drona's consecration)","verses":[{"text":"धृतराष्ट्र उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Dhritarashtra said:"}},{"n":1,"text":"शृणु दिव्यानि कर्माणि वासुदेवस्य संजय ।\nकृतवान्यानि गोविन्दो यथा नान्यः पुमान्क्वचित् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Listen, Sanjaya, to the divine deeds of Vasudeva, which Govinda performed as no other man has anywhere."}},{"n":2,"text":"संवर्धता गोपकुले बालेनैव महात्मना ।\nविख्यापितं बलं बाह्वोस्त्रिषु लोकेषु संजय ॥","meaning":{"en":"While still a boy growing up among the cowherds, the great soul made known the strength of his arms in the three worlds, Sanjaya."}},{"n":3,"text":"उच्चैःश्रवस्तुल्यबलं वायुवेगसमं जवे ।\nजघान हयराजं यो यमुनावनवासिनम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"He killed the king of horses who lived in the Yamuna forest, equal to Uchchaihshravas in strength and like the wind in speed."}},{"n":4,"text":"दानवं घोरकर्माणं गवां मृत्युमिवोत्थितम् ।\nवृषरूपधरं बाल्ये भुजाभ्यां निजघान ह ॥","meaning":{"en":"He killed with his arms, while still a boy, a terrible danava in the form of a bull, who had arisen like death for the cattle."}},{"n":5,"text":"प्रलम्बं नरकं जम्भं पीठं चापि महासुरम् ।\nमुरुं चाचलसंकाशमवधीत्पुष्करेक्षणः ॥","meaning":{"en":"The lotus-eyed one killed Pralamba, Naraka, Jambha and Pitha, the great asuras, and Mura, who was like a mountain."}},{"n":6,"text":"तथा कंसो महातेजा जरासंधेन पालितः ।\nविक्रमेणैव कृष्णेन सगणः शातितो रणे ॥","meaning":{"en":"So too Kamsa, of great brilliance and sustained by Jarasandha, was destroyed in battle with his followers by Krishna's valor alone."}},{"n":7,"text":"सुनामा नाम विक्रान्तः समग्राक्षौहिणीपतिः ।\nभोजराजस्य मध्यस्थो भ्राता कंसस्य वीर्यवान् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Sunama, a valiant lord of a whole akshauhini, the strong brother of Kamsa, king of the Bhojas, standing in the middle of the family,"}},{"n":8,"text":"बलदेवद्वितीयेन कृष्णेनामित्रघातिना ।\nतरस्वी समरे दग्धः ससैन्यः शूरसेनराट् ॥","meaning":{"en":"was burned in battle, with his army, the swift king of the Shurasenas, by Krishna, the slayer of foes, with Baladeva as his second."}},{"n":9,"text":"दुर्वासा नाम विप्रर्षिस्तथा परमकोपनः ।\nआराधितः सदारेण स चास्मै प्रददौ वरान् ॥","meaning":{"en":"The brahmin sage Durvasa, who was extremely irascible, was served by him and his wife, and gave him boons."}},{"n":10,"text":"तथा गान्धारराजस्य सुतां वीरः स्वयंवरे ।\nनिर्जित्य पृथिवीपालानवहत्पुष्करेक्षणः ॥","meaning":{"en":"The lotus-eyed hero also defeated the kings at the svayamvara of the Gandhara king's daughter and carried her off."}},{"n":11,"text":"अमृष्यमाणा राजानो यस्य जात्या हया इव ।\nरथे वैवाहिके युक्ताः प्रतोदेन कृतव्रणाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Those kings, unable to bear it, were like horses yoked to a wedding chariot, with weals made by his whip."}},{"n":12,"text":"जरासंधं महाबाहुमुपायेन जनार्दनः ।\nपरेण घातयामास पृथगक्षौहिणीपतिम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"By a stratagem, Janardana had Jarasandha, mighty-armed lord of an akshauhini, killed by another."}},{"n":13,"text":"चेदिराजं च विक्रान्तं राजसेनापतिं बली ।\nअर्घे विवदमानं च जघान पशुवत्तदा ॥","meaning":{"en":"The mighty one also killed the valiant king of Chedi, commander of kings, like a sacrificial animal, when he quarreled about the honor offering."}},{"n":14,"text":"सौभं दैत्यपुरं स्वस्थं शाल्वगुप्तं दुरासदम् ।\nसमुद्रकुक्षौ विक्रम्य पातयामास माधवः ॥","meaning":{"en":"The Saubha, a city of the daityas, set in the air, protected by Shalva and hard to reach, Madhava brought down by his valor into the belly of the ocean."}},{"n":15,"text":"अङ्गान्वङ्गान्कलिङ्गांश्च मागधान्काशिकोसलान् ।\nवत्सगर्गकरूषांश्च पुण्ड्रांश्चाप्यजयद्रणे ॥","meaning":{"en":"He conquered in battle the Angas, Vangas, Kalingas, Magadhas, Kashis, Kosalas, Vatsas, Gargas, Karushas and Pundras."}},{"n":16,"text":"आवन्त्यान्दाक्षिणात्यांश्च पार्वतीयान्दशेरकान् ।\nकाश्मीरकानौरसकान्पिशाचांश्च समन्दरान् ॥","meaning":{"en":"He also conquered the Avantis, southerners, mountain people, Dasherakas, Kashmirakas, Aurasakas, Pishachas and Samandaras."}},{"n":17,"text":"काम्बोजान्वाटधानांश्च चोलान्पाण्ड्यांश्च संजय ।\nत्रिगर्तान्मालवांश्चैव दरदांश्च सुदुर्जयान् ॥","meaning":{"en":"The Kambojas, Vatadhanas, Cholas and Pandyas, Sanjaya, the Trigartas, Malavas and the very hard to conquer Daradas,"}},{"n":18,"text":"नानादिग्भ्यश्च संप्राप्तान्व्रातानश्वशकान्प्रति ।\nजितवान्पुण्डरीकाक्षो यवनांश्च सहानुगान् ॥","meaning":{"en":"and the hordes of Shakas and Yavanas with their followers who had come from many directions, the lotus-eyed one defeated."}},{"n":19,"text":"प्रविश्य मकरावासं यादोभिरभिसंवृतम् ।\nजिगाय वरुणं युद्धे सलिलान्तर्गतं पुरा ॥","meaning":{"en":"He entered the abode of the sea monster, thronged with sea creatures, and long ago defeated Varuna in battle, who was within the waters."}},{"n":20,"text":"युधि पञ्चजनं हत्वा पातालतलवासिनम् ।\nपाञ्चजन्यं हृषीकेशो दिव्यं शङ्खमवाप्तवान् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Having killed Panchajana, who lived in the depths of the netherworld, in battle, Hrishikesha obtained the divine conch Panchajanya."}},{"n":21,"text":"खाण्डवे पार्थसहितस्तोषयित्वा हुताशनम् ।\nआग्नेयमस्त्रं दुर्धर्षं चक्रं लेभे महाबलः ॥","meaning":{"en":"At Khandava, together with Partha, the strong one satisfied Agni and obtained the unassailable discus, a weapon of fire."}},{"n":22,"text":"वैनतेयं समारुह्य त्रासयित्वामरावतीम् ।\nमहेन्द्रभवनाद्वीरः पारिजातमुपानयत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Mounting Garuda, Vinata's son, and frightening Amaravati, the hero brought the Parijata tree from Mahendra's abode."}},{"n":23,"text":"तच्च मर्षितवाञ्शक्रो जानंस्तस्य पराक्रमम् ।\nराज्ञां चाप्यजितं कंचित्कृष्णेनेह न शुश्रुम ॥","meaning":{"en":"Shakra endured that, knowing his valor, and we have not heard of any king whom Krishna failed to conquer here."}},{"n":24,"text":"यच्च तन्महदाश्चर्यं सभायां मम संजय ।\nकृतवान्पुण्डरीकाक्षः कस्तदन्य इहार्हति ॥","meaning":{"en":"The great marvel that the lotus-eyed one worked in my assembly, Sanjaya, who else here could do it?"}},{"n":25,"text":"यच्च भक्त्या प्रपन्नोऽहमद्राक्षं कृष्णमीश्वरम् ।\nतन्मे सुविदितं सर्वं प्रत्यक्षमिव चागमत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"And what I saw when I approached Krishna the lord with devotion, all that I know well, as if before my eyes."}},{"n":26,"text":"नान्तो विक्रमयुक्तस्य बुद्ध्या युक्तस्य वा पुनः ।\nकर्मणः शक्यते गन्तुं हृषीकेशस्य संजय ॥","meaning":{"en":"There is no end to the action of Hrishikesha, who is endowed with valor and wisdom, Sanjaya."}},{"n":27,"text":"तथा गदश्च साम्बश्च प्रद्युम्नोऽथ विदूरथः ।\nआगावहोऽनिरुद्धश्च चारुदेष्णश्च सारणः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Gada, Samba, Pradyumna, Vidurtha, Agavaha, Aniruddha, Charudeshna, Sarana,"}},{"n":28,"text":"उल्मुको निशठश्चैव झल्ली बभ्रुश्च वीर्यवान् ।\nपृथुश्च विपृथुश्चैव समीकोऽथारिमेजयः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Ulmuka, Nishatha, Jhalli, the strong Babhru, Prithu, Viprithu, Samika and Arimejaya,"}},{"n":29,"text":"एते वै बलवन्तश्च वृष्णिवीराः प्रहारिणः ।\nकथंचित्पाण्डवानीकं श्रयेयुः समरे स्थिताः ॥","meaning":{"en":"these mighty Vrishni heroes, strong strikers, might somehow side with the Pandava army and stand in battle."}},{"n":30,"text":"आहूता वृष्णिवीरेण केशवेन महात्मना ।\nततः संशयितं सर्वं भवेदिति मतिर्मम ॥","meaning":{"en":"If they were summoned by Keshava, the great-souled Vrishni hero, then I think everything would hang in doubt."}},{"n":31,"text":"नागायुतबलो वीरः कैलासशिखरोपमः ।\nवनमाली हली रामस्तत्र यत्र जनार्दनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Rama, strong as ten thousand elephants, like a peak of Kailasa, the garland-wearer and plough-bearer, is wherever Janardana is."}},{"n":32,"text":"यमाहुः सर्वपितरं वासुदेवं द्विजातयः ।\nअपि वा ह्येष पाण्डूनां योत्स्यतेऽर्थाय संजय ॥","meaning":{"en":"Whom the twice-born call the father of all, Vasudeva, may even fight for the sake of the Pandavas, Sanjaya."}},{"n":33,"text":"स यदा तात संनह्येत्पाण्डवार्थाय केशवः ।\nन तदा प्रत्यनीकेषु भविता तस्य कश्चन ॥","meaning":{"en":"When Keshava girds himself for the Pandavas, dear Sanjaya, no one among their opponents will stand against him."}},{"n":34,"text":"यदि स्म कुरवः सर्वे जयेयुः सर्वपाण्डवान् ।\nवार्ष्णेयोऽर्थाय तेषां वै गृह्णीयाच्छस्त्रमुत्तमम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"If all the Kurus were to conquer all the Pandavas, the Vrishni would take up his best weapon for them."}},{"n":35,"text":"ततः सर्वान्नरव्याघ्रो हत्वा नरपतीन्रणे ।\nकौरवांश्च महाबाहुः कुन्त्यै दद्यात्स मेदिनीम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then that mighty-armed tiger among men would kill all the kings and Kauravas in battle and give the earth to Kunti."}},{"n":36,"text":"यस्य यन्ता हृषीकेशो योद्धा यस्य धनंजयः ।\nरथस्य तस्य कः संख्ये प्रत्यनीको भवेद्रथः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Whose charioteer is Hrishikesha and whose fighter is Dhananjaya, what chariot in battle could face that chariot?"}},{"n":37,"text":"न केनचिदुपायेन कुरूणां दृश्यते जयः ।\nतस्मान्मे सर्वमाचक्ष्व यथा युद्धमवर्तत ॥","meaning":{"en":"In no way do I see victory for the Kurus. So tell me everything of how the battle went."}},{"n":38,"text":"अर्जुनः केशवस्यात्मा कृष्णोऽप्यात्मा किरीटिनः ।\nअर्जुने विजयो नित्यं कृष्णे कीर्तिश्च शाश्वती ॥","meaning":{"en":"Arjuna is the soul of Keshava, and Krishna is the soul of the diademed one. Victory is always in Arjuna, and eternal fame in Krishna."}},{"n":39,"text":"प्राधान्येन हि भूयिष्ठममेयाः केशवे गुणाः ।\nमोहाद्दुर्योधनः कृष्णं यन्न वेत्तीह माधवम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Keshava's qualities are chiefly immeasurable. Duryodhana, in delusion, does not know Krishna as Madhava here."}},{"n":40,"text":"मोहितो दैवयोगेन मृत्युपाशपुरस्कृतः ।\nन वेद कृष्णं दाशार्हमर्जुनं चैव पाण्डवम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Deluded by the working of fate, with the noose of death before him, he does not know Krishna the Dasharha nor the Pandava Arjuna."}},{"n":41,"text":"पूर्वदेवौ महात्मानौ नरनारायणावुभौ ।\nएकात्मानौ द्विधाभूतौ दृश्येते मानवैर्भुवि ॥","meaning":{"en":"The two great-souled ones, Nara and Narayana, the former gods, are one soul made two and are seen by men on earth."}},{"n":42,"text":"मनसापि हि दुर्धर्षौ सेनामेतां यशस्विनौ ।\nनाशयेतामिहेच्छन्तौ मानुषत्वात्तु नेच्छतः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Those two glorious ones, hard to assault even in thought, could destroy this army here if they wished, but out of their human nature they do not wish to."}},{"n":43,"text":"युगस्येव विपर्यासो लोकानामिव मोहनम् ।\nभीष्मस्य च वधस्तात द्रोणस्य च महात्मनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Like the reversal of an age, like the bewilderment of the worlds, dear one, is the killing of Bhishma and of great-souled Drona."}},{"n":44,"text":"न ह्येव ब्रह्मचर्येण न वेदाध्ययनेन च ।\nन क्रियाभिर्न शस्त्रेण मृत्योः कश्चिद्विमुच्यते ॥","meaning":{"en":"Neither by chastity, nor by Vedic study, nor by rites, nor by weapons, does anyone escape death."}},{"n":45,"text":"लोकसंभावितौ वीरौ कृतास्त्रौ युद्धदुर्मदौ ।\nभीष्मद्रोणौ हतौ श्रुत्वा किं नु जीवामि संजय ॥","meaning":{"en":"Hearing that Bhishma and Drona, respected by the world, trained in weapons and wild in battle, are slain, how can I still live, Sanjaya?"}},{"n":46,"text":"यां तां श्रियमसूयामः पुरा यातां युधिष्ठिरे ।\nअद्य तामनुजानीमो भीष्मद्रोणवधेन च ॥","meaning":{"en":"The prosperity that went to Yudhishthira earlier, and which we begrudged, we now acknowledge, with the deaths of Bhishma and Drona."}},{"n":47,"text":"तथा च मत्कृते प्राप्तः कुरूणामेष संक्षयः ।\nपक्वानां हि वधे सूत वज्रायन्ते तृणान्यपि ॥","meaning":{"en":"And so, because of me, this destruction of the Kurus has come. When the ripe are cut down, even grass becomes like a thunderbolt."}},{"n":48,"text":"अनन्यमिदमैश्वर्यं लोके प्राप्तो युधिष्ठिरः ।\nयस्य कोपान्महेष्वासौ भीष्मद्रोणौ निपातितौ ॥","meaning":{"en":"Yudhishthira has gained in this world a sovereignty like none other, by whose anger the great archers Bhishma and Drona were felled."}},{"n":49,"text":"प्राप्तः प्रकृतितो धर्मो नाधर्मो मानवान्प्रति ।\nक्रूरः सर्वविनाशाय कालः समतिवर्तते ॥","meaning":{"en":"By nature, dharma comes to men, not adharma. Cruel time moves on for the destruction of all."}},{"n":50,"text":"अन्यथा चिन्तिता ह्यर्था नरैस्तात मनस्विभिः ।\nअन्यथैव हि गच्छन्ति दैवादिति मतिर्मम ॥","meaning":{"en":"Dear one, matters men of spirit have planned in one way go another way by fate, so I think."}},{"n":51,"text":"तस्मादपरिहार्येऽर्थे संप्राप्ते कृच्छ्र उत्तमे ।\nअपारणीये दुश्चिन्त्ये यथाभूतं प्रचक्ष्व मे ॥","meaning":{"en":"Therefore, now that an unavoidable event has come, the worst hardship, unbearable and hard to think of, tell me just as it happened."}}]}]}